From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 16:55:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: advertise what this modem can actually do over IMS

Three device-capability booleans, the carrier legs that gate them, and the CarrierConfig bundle for
T-Mobile US. One patch, because they are one decision expressed in four files, and splitting them
across the series made the end state unreadable: a reader had to hold four patches in their head to
learn what one boolean ends up as.

The device leg lives unqualified in values/config.xml and deliberately NOT under an mcc/mnc
qualifier. It used to, and that was the wrong axis: ImsManager.isVolteEnabledByPlatform() ANDs the
device leg with the carrier's carrier_volte_available_bool, so qualifying the device leg by carrier
refused every network except the two we had directories for, before that network's own carrier config
was ever consulted -- including carriers AOSP ships working VoLTE config for. Whether this hardware
can do VoLTE does not depend on which SIM is inserted. Carrier permission is the carrier leg's job.

Android also resolves those qualifiers from the SIM, not from the serving network. Mint runs on
T-Mobile, so gsm.sim.operator.numeric reads 310240 while gsm.operator.numeric reads 310260, and a
value placed only under mnc260 never applies to a Mint SIM. Both directories therefore carry the
genuinely per-carrier legs, and only those.

volte true. vt false: lib-imsvt.so imports IOMXObserver and IGraphicBufferAlloc among 61 unresolved
symbols, platform interfaces deleted outright when OMX moved to HIDL/Codec2, so the engine cannot be
shimmed back. False removes the carrier video-calling toggle and stops the framework requesting a VT
capability at all.

The carrier leg says the same: carrier_vt_available_bool is false too. ImsManager ANDs the two, so
true there was inert, but a carrier config advertising a capability the device denies is a trap for
whoever reads it next.

wfc false, because it cannot work on this hardware and not because it was not tried. The framework
side is complete and the modem's EFS is provisioned for iWLAN as fully as a handset that sells the
feature, but the modem never attempts an ePDG tunnel, and a later modem build cannot be loaded: it
asks PIL for a 100 MB relocatable region against a 90 MB modem_mem reservation that cannot grow,
because peripheral_mem ends exactly where modem_mem begins. True here produces a toggle that appears
and then fails every time, which is worse than no toggle. Full account in VOLTE-BRINGUP.md section 8.

The structure stays wired so another device inherits it by flipping one boolean.
---
 .../res/res/values-mcc310-mnc240/config.xml   | 17 +++++++++
 .../res/res/values-mcc310-mnc260/config.xml   | 17 +++++++++
 .../base/core/res/res/values/config.xml       | 25 +++++++++++++
 .../apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml     | 35 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 94 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc240/config.xml
 create mode 100644 overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc260/config.xml
 create mode 100644 overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml

diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc240/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc240/config.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b18ed8e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc240/config.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- Mint Mobile (MCC 310 / MNC 240). Carrier-specific legs only.
+
+     The device-capability booleans (config_device_volte_available and friends) are NOT here: they
+     live unqualified in values/config.xml, because whether this modem can do VoLTE does not depend
+     on the SIM. Only genuinely per-carrier values belong in an mcc/mnc directory.
+
+     Worth keeping in mind for anything added here: Android resolves these qualifiers from the SIM,
+     not from the serving network. Mint runs on T-Mobile, so gsm.sim.operator.numeric reads 310240
+     while gsm.operator.numeric reads 310260, and a value placed only under mnc260 never applies to
+     a Mint SIM. That cost this port a long time when the device leg lived here. -->
+<resources>
+    <!-- legacy carrier leg some code paths still consult -->
+    <bool name="config_carrier_volte_available">true</bool>
+    <!-- displayed RAT during a VoLTE call; 3 = UMTS, T-Mobile's value -->
+    <integer name="config_volte_replacement_rat">3</integer>
+</resources>
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc260/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc260/config.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a1fc5dc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc310-mnc260/config.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<!-- T-Mobile US (MCC 310 / MNC 260). Carrier-specific legs only.
+
+     The device-capability booleans (config_device_volte_available and friends) are NOT here: they
+     live unqualified in values/config.xml, because whether this modem can do VoLTE does not depend
+     on the SIM. Only genuinely per-carrier values belong in an mcc/mnc directory.
+
+     Worth keeping in mind for anything added here: Android resolves these qualifiers from the SIM,
+     not from the serving network. Mint runs on T-Mobile, so gsm.sim.operator.numeric reads 310240
+     while gsm.operator.numeric reads 310260, and a value placed only under mnc260 never applies to
+     a Mint SIM. That cost this port a long time when the device leg lived here. -->
+<resources>
+    <!-- legacy carrier leg some code paths still consult -->
+    <bool name="config_carrier_volte_available">true</bool>
+    <!-- displayed RAT during a VoLTE call; 3 = UMTS, T-Mobile's value -->
+    <integer name="config_volte_replacement_rat">3</integer>
+</resources>
diff --git a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
index b58855e..1b90e6c 100644
--- a/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -281,4 +281,29 @@
          colon-separated *string*; a string-array is silently ignored. -->
     <string name="config_defaultListenerAccessPackages" translatable="false">com.nextbit.robinled</string>
 
+    <!-- IMS device capability. This is the "can this hardware do it" leg, and it has nothing to do
+         with which SIM is inserted, so it is deliberately NOT under an mcc/mnc qualifier.
+
+         It used to be, and that was the wrong axis: ImsManager.isVolteEnabledByPlatform() ANDs this
+         with the carrier's carrier_volte_available_bool, so qualifying the device leg by carrier
+         meant every network except the two we had directories for was refused before its own
+         carrier config was ever consulted, including carriers AOSP ships working VoLTE config for.
+         Carrier permission is the carrier leg's job.
+
+         Video calling is off deliberately, not merely untested: lib-imsvt.so imports IOMXObserver
+         and IGraphicBufferAlloc, platform interfaces deleted outright when OMX moved to HIDL and
+         Codec2, among 61 unresolved symbols, and they are not shimmable. libshim_vtsurface exists
+         only so ImsVideoGlobals.init() can construct its singletons. False here removes the carrier
+         video calling toggle and stops the framework requesting a VT capability at all. -->
+    <bool name="config_device_volte_available">true</bool>
+    <bool name="config_device_vt_available">false</bool>
+    <!-- Wi-Fi calling is false because it cannot work on this hardware, not because it was not
+         tried. The framework side is complete and the modem's own EFS is provisioned for iWLAN as
+         fully as a handset that sells the feature, but the modem never attempts an ePDG tunnel, and a
+         later modem build cannot be loaded: it asks PIL for a 100 MB relocatable region against a
+         90 MB modem_mem reservation that cannot grow, because peripheral_mem ends exactly where it
+         begins. True here only produces a toggle that appears and then fails every time, which is
+         worse than no toggle. Full account in VOLTE-BRINGUP.md section 8. -->
+    <bool name="config_device_wfc_ims_available">false</bool>
+
 </resources>
diff --git a/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e3b221a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/overlay/packages/apps/CarrierConfig/res/xml/vendor.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8' standalone='yes' ?>
+<!-- CarrierConfig overlay: enable VoLTE / VT / Wi-Fi Calling for T-Mobile US ONLY
+     (MCC 310 / MNC 260, includes Mint Mobile). The mcc+mnc filter scopes this bundle to that
+     network; every other carrier keeps its AOSP/assets defaults (the stock vendor.xml was an
+     empty <carrier_config_list/>). This is the authoritative A11 availability leg:
+     carrier_volte_available_bool is ANDed with config_device_volte_available in ImsManager.
+     Whether IMS actually registers is then up to the network — T-Mobile also gates IMS behind
+     a device whitelist, so this may still no-op on ether. Add more T-Mobile MNCs as sibling
+     <carrier_config> blocks if a SIM reports something other than 310/260. -->
+<carrier_config_list>
+    <carrier_config mcc="310" mnc="260">
+        <boolean name="carrier_volte_available_bool" value="true" />
+        <boolean name="carrier_vt_available_bool" value="false" />
+        <boolean name="carrier_wfc_ims_available_bool" value="false" />
+        <boolean name="enhanced_4g_lte_on_by_default_bool" value="true" />
+        <boolean name="editable_enhanced_4g_lte_bool" value="true" />
+        <boolean name="editable_wfc_mode_bool" value="false" />
+        <boolean name="carrier_volte_provisioning_required_bool" value="false" />
+        <boolean name="carrier_ims_gba_required_bool" value="false" />
+        <boolean name="carrier_volte_override_wfc_provisioning_bool" value="true" />
+        <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_mode_int" value="1" />
+        <int name="carrier_default_wfc_ims_roaming_mode_int" value="1" />
+
+        <!-- Wi-Fi calling needs IMS provisioning required for VOICE over IWLAN, or the modem is
+             never told the feature is provisioned and declines every attempt to configure it. That
+             is NOT set here, deliberately: it needs a nested <pbundle_as_map>, and this file is
+             parsed by PersistableBundle.restoreFromXml() with throwException=false, so a nested
+             bundle it cannot handle is dropped in silence. The XML compiles into the APK correctly
+             and simply never reaches the merged config; every scalar around it applies, which
+             makes it look like it worked.
+
+             It lives in frameworks/base instead, as the default for
+             Ims.KEY_MMTEL_REQUIRES_PROVISIONING_BUNDLE. See that patch. -->
+    </carrier_config>
+</carrier_config_list>
